# Cursor IDE Rules for PBX Voice System Development

## Project Overview
You are building a complete PBX (Private Branch Exchange) voice system similar to GoToConnect using only open-source technologies. The system includes a softphone with WebRTC, admin panel, and ELK stack monitoring.

## Technology Stack

### Backend
- **Go (Fiber)** - High-performance HTTP API server
- **PostgreSQL** - Primary database for structured data
- **Redis** - Caching and session management
- **Freeswitch** - Core telephony engine with mod_xml_curl integration

### Frontend
- **React/TypeScript** - Modern admin interface and softphone
- **Tailwind CSS** - Utility-first CSS framework
- **SIP.js** - WebRTC softphone implementation

### Monitoring & Analytics
- **OpenSearch** - Elasticsearch alternative for log aggregation
- **Logstash** - Log processing and transformation
- **Kibana** - Data visualization and dashboards

### Infrastructure
- **Docker** - Containerization and orchestration
- **Nginx** - Reverse proxy and load balancer
- **Let's Encrypt** - SSL certificate management

## Code Standards & Best Practices

### Go Backend Development
- Use Fiber framework for HTTP server implementation
- Follow Go naming conventions: camelCase for variables, PascalCase for exported names
- Use GORM for database operations with proper migrations
- Implement comprehensive error handling with custom error types
- Use context for cancellation and timeouts in all operations
- Structure code into: controllers, services, models, middleware, routes
- Use environment variables for all configuration
- Implement structured logging with proper log levels
- Use dependency injection pattern for services
- Write unit tests for all business logic
- Use interfaces for better testability and modularity

### React Frontend Development
- Use TypeScript for type safety throughout the application
- Use functional components with React hooks (useState, useEffect, useContext)
- Use Tailwind CSS for responsive and modern styling
- Implement proper state management using Context API or Redux Toolkit
- Use React Router for navigation and routing
- Implement proper error boundaries for error handling
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for API responses and props
- Implement proper form validation using libraries like react-hook-form
- Use React.memo for performance optimization
- Implement proper loading states and error handling
- Use proper accessibility attributes (aria-labels, roles)

### Database Design & Management
- Use PostgreSQL as the primary database for all structured data
- Use Redis for caching, sessions, and real-time data
- Implement proper database migrations using GORM
- Use connection pooling for database connections
- Implement proper indexing strategies for performance
- Use transactions for data consistency
- Implement proper backup and recovery procedures
- Use proper database normalization
- Implement proper foreign key relationships
- Use proper data types and constraints

### Telephony Integration (Freeswitch)
- Use Freeswitch as the core telephony engine
- Implement mod_xml_curl for dynamic configuration management
- Use ESL (Event Socket Library) for real-time event handling
- Implement proper SIP protocol handling
- Use WebRTC for softphone functionality
- Implement proper call routing and management
- Use proper media handling and codec optimization
- Implement proper call recording and voicemail features
- Use proper security measures for SIP communication
- Implement proper call queuing and IVR systems

### WebRTC & Softphone Implementation
- Use SIP.js library for SIP protocol implementation
- Implement proper WebRTC media handling
- Use STUN/TURN servers for NAT traversal
- Implement proper media codec optimization
- Use proper security measures for WebRTC
- Implement proper call quality monitoring
- Use proper error handling for connection issues
- Implement proper user interface for call controls
- Use proper audio/video device management
- Implement proper call history and contact management

### Monitoring & Logging (ELK Stack)
- Use OpenSearch for centralized log aggregation
- Use Logstash for log processing and transformation
- Use Kibana for data visualization and dashboards
- Implement structured logging throughout the application
- Monitor system performance and call quality metrics
- Implement proper alerting and notification systems
- Use proper log retention and archival policies
- Implement proper security for log data
- Use proper log parsing and filtering
- Implement proper dashboard creation for different stakeholders

## Project Structure

### Recommended Directory Structure
```
pbx-voice-system/
├── .vscode/                    # Cursor IDE configuration
│   ├── settings.json
│   ├── tasks.json
│   ├── launch.json
│   └── extensions.json
├── backend/                    # Go API server
│   ├── cmd/                   # Application entry point
│   ├── controllers/           # HTTP request handlers
│   ├── services/              # Business logic layer
│   ├── models/                # Data models and structs
│   ├── middleware/            # HTTP middleware
│   ├── routes/                # Route definitions
│   ├── database/              # Database migrations and setup
│   ├── utils/                 # Utility functions
│   ├── config/                # Configuration management
│   └── tests/                 # Unit and integration tests
├── frontend/                  # React admin panel
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/        # Reusable React components
│   │   ├── pages/             # Page components
│   │   ├── services/          # API service layer
│   │   ├── hooks/             # Custom React hooks
│   │   ├── utils/             # Utility functions
│   │   ├── types/             # TypeScript type definitions
│   │   ├── styles/            # CSS and styling
│   │   └── assets/            # Static assets
│   ├── public/                # Public assets
│   └── tests/                 # Frontend tests
├── softphone/                 # WebRTC softphone
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/        # Phone-specific components
│   │   ├── services/          # SIP and WebRTC services
│   │   ├── hooks/             # Custom hooks for phone
│   │   ├── utils/             # Phone utilities
│   │   └── types/             # Phone type definitions
│   ├── public/                # Public assets
│   └── tests/                 # Softphone tests
├── freeswitch/                # Freeswitch configuration
│   ├── conf/                  # Configuration files
│   ├── scripts/               # Custom scripts
│   └── recordings/            # Call recordings
├── monitoring/                # ELK stack configuration
│   ├── logstash/              # Log processing configuration
│   ├── kibana/                # Dashboard configurations
│   └── opensearch/            # Search engine configuration
├── docker/                    # Docker configurations
│   ├── nginx/                 # Reverse proxy configuration
│   ├── ssl/                   # SSL certificates
│   └── scripts/               # Docker utility scripts
├── docs/                      # Documentation
├── scripts/                   # Build and deployment scripts
├── docker-compose.yml         # Development environment
├── docker-compose.prod.yml    # Production environment
├── go.mod                     # Go module definition
├── package.json               # Node.js dependencies
└── README.md                  # Project documentation
```

